.SH NAME
lmm-deploy - Deploy mods to game directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm deploy [mod-id] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deploy mod files from cache to game directory.

.PP
Use this when changing deployment methods (symlink, hardlink, copy)
or if mod files need to be refreshed.

.PP
Without a mod ID, deploys all enabled mods in the current profile.
With a mod ID, deploys only that specific mod; -s/--source then identifies
which source that mod ID belongs to - it resolves automatically when the
game has exactly one configured source, or prompts interactively when it
has several. -s is ignored when deploying the whole profile.

.PP
Use --purge to remove all deployed mods before deploying. This ensures
a clean slate, useful when mods have gotten out of sync.

.PP
Use --all to deploy all mods including disabled ones (e.g., after a purge).

.PP
Examples:
  lmm deploy --game skyrim-se
  lmm deploy --game skyrim-se --all
  lmm deploy --game skyrim-se --method hardlink
  lmm deploy --game skyrim-se --purge
  lmm deploy 12345 --game skyrim-se
  lmm deploy 12345 --game skyrim-se --source curseforge
  lmm deploy 12345 --game skyrim-se --method copy


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--all\fP[=false]
	deploy all mods including disabled ones

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--force\fP[=false]
	continue even if hooks fail

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for deploy

.PP
\fB-m\fP, \fB--method\fP=""
	link method: symlink, hardlink, or copy (default: game's configured method)

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB--purge\fP[=false]
	purge all deployed mods before deploying

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--source\fP=""
	mod source for deploying a single mod ID (default: auto-detect when the game has one configured source, prompt when it has several)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output in JSON format (list, status, search, update, conflicts, verify, mod show, source list, game list)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


